---
description: Report PACE-CSAT results as associations, with their uncertainty, never as causes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Associations, not causes

- The data is observational. Write "restaurants with higher PACE Hospitality tend to have higher CSAT Hospitality", not "improving PACE raises CSAT" or "PACE drives CSAT".
- Avoid "impact", "effect of", "drives", "leads to", and "because of" for PACE-CSAT relationships. Regression slopes are "associated differences", for example "+10 pp PACE is associated with +2 pp CSAT".
- Quote an estimate with its n and CI (or q-value) the first time it appears.
- When pooled and within-market results differ, lead with the within-market result and say why the pooled one misleads.
- A null or weak result is a finding. Report it rather than searching for a cut that "works"; every extra cut is a follow-up that goes through FDR.
